* Pinned ngspice environment -- staged into every run directory by
* sim/lib (issue #338). A run-directory .spiceinit replaces $HOME/.spiceinit,
* so every setting a run needs is in this file. Single source of truth:
* SPICEINIT_TEXT in sim/lib/deck_adapter.py; do not edit copies.
*
* ngbehavior=hsa: the mode the committed sim/ corpus ran under (its corner
* logs carry 'Compatibility modes selected: hs a'), so the committed records
* stay reproducible, and the mode the gf180mcu ngspice model decks are
* written against (a distro-packaged ngspice supplies it via its own spinit;
* a locally built one does not).
set ngbehavior=hsa
* One ngspice thread per unit: batch-fleet workers run units in parallel
* and rely on per-worker thread pinning; a run-directory .spiceinit would
* otherwise drop the host's num_threads and oversubscribe a shared worker.
set num_threads=1
* Per-finger model binning (W/NF). NOT implied by ngbehavior=hsa (verified
* 2026-11-14, #338). Inert today -- every device in this repo is nf=1, so
* W/nf == W and bin selection cannot change -- but pinned so drawing a
* multi-finger device cannot silently change model-bin selection.
set wnflag=1
